rds still in hand.\n\nReason:\nMy teammate has only 9 cards remaining compared to my 17, and they intentionally played a low single card (♦5) after winning the previous trick. This suggests they want to keep playing and potentially go out soon. As a peasant, my role is to help my teammate win, not necessarily to win myself. By passing, I either force the landlord to play (which creates opportunities for my teammate) or allow my teammate to regain control if the landlord passes. Taking control now with 17 cards would be counterproductive to our team strategy.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
